{
  "$note": "The names of the identity documents in `identity_document_types`. Composed at runtime from the catalogue's `label_key`, so the family is declared in composed-keys.json.\n\nMost entries also carry a `label_verbatim` — CUIT, CNPJ, RUC — which WINS over the value here: those are the words the authority prints on the paper the user is copying from, and a translated gloss makes them harder to find, not easier. The values below are the fallback, and they are what a reader sees for an entry whose catalogue row leaves `label_verbatim` null.\n\nThese keys replace `hcm.employees.form.document_type.cedula` and `.rnc`, which were not translations at all: the regional patches used them to RENAME the same enum value per locale — 'SSN' in en-US, 'RUN' in es-CL, 'CPF' in pt-BR — while the server validated every one of them with the Dominican algorithms.",

